WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.940
An empty castle
ruled by willful neglect

00:02.120 --> 00:03.940
Attack on sight.

00:04.240 --> 00:06.430
I repeat: attack these two on sight.

00:06.430 --> 00:08.520
Your gambling losses will be erased.

00:09.030 --> 00:10.750
You'll earn ten thousand dollars
for any injury inflicted on them.

00:11.080 --> 00:12.750
One million dollars if you kill them.

00:15.520 --> 00:19.750
You assholes must <i>really</i> want to die.

00:20.210 --> 00:22.750
Oh, no.

01:53.430 --> 01:54.400
Tachihara.

01:54.400 --> 01:55.180
Yes, sir.

01:55.180 --> 01:58.930
We, police, must never hurt
civilians, no matter what.

01:59.230 --> 02:01.380
And we will achieve our objectives.

02:01.380 --> 02:02.520
Yes, sir!

02:14.250 --> 02:15.870
'Ey, old lady.

02:15.870 --> 02:17.200
Eh?

02:17.200 --> 02:18.730
Did two people pass through here?

02:18.730 --> 02:20.290
Huh?

02:20.290 --> 02:21.030
Hey!

02:22.390 --> 02:23.410
Take a look at this.

02:25.530 --> 02:27.520
They went to the lower deck!

02:27.520 --> 02:28.370
Hurry!

02:28.370 --> 02:29.500
They're downstairs!

02:30.210 --> 02:31.690
Let our friends know downstairs.

02:31.690 --> 02:32.540
Right.

02:34.320 --> 02:35.790
The enemy's downstairs!

02:36.600 --> 02:38.210
The bounty's mine!

02:46.260 --> 02:47.850
What do you want, old woman?

02:47.850 --> 02:49.820
You aren't allowed here.

02:49.820 --> 02:52.580
Oh, really?

02:52.580 --> 02:55.160
Are we getting simmered
flounder for dinner tonight?

02:55.160 --> 02:57.510
What are you doing all the way down here?

02:57.510 --> 02:59.810
Oh, what was it again...?

03:00.760 --> 03:03.270
Ah, I remember!

03:03.750 --> 03:05.740
I remember now!

03:11.240 --> 03:14.420
I came to beat the shit out
of you wretched criminals.

03:14.420 --> 03:15.910
Um...

03:17.700 --> 03:19.540
Can I get out, now?

03:21.490 --> 03:24.910
You ought to come to the
next company party like that.

03:24.910 --> 03:26.770
Please, no!

03:29.970 --> 03:33.420
My ability allows me to control age.

03:33.420 --> 03:36.540
Now, I'll ask before you
become hard of hearing.

03:36.930 --> 03:41.040
How do I take control of the
central control terminal ahead?

03:41.390 --> 03:44.410
Don't worry. I won't kill you.

03:44.410 --> 03:48.170
I'll stop right around when
you start severe joint pains.

03:48.570 --> 03:52.210
That's the most feared ability
in the Hunting Dogs.

03:52.460 --> 03:59.140
Even the toughest of men can stand being
tortured after being made elderly or infant.

04:01.610 --> 04:07.310
The terminal has to be reset with a key.

04:07.310 --> 04:09.460
The manager has the only one.

04:11.720 --> 04:12.850
Good.

04:14.000 --> 04:16.990
There'll be more security here soon.

04:16.990 --> 04:19.400
It'll be your job to stop them.

04:19.790 --> 04:20.790
What about you?

04:22.990 --> 04:25.270
I'll take the king's head.

04:25.280 --> 04:28.280
Episode 50

04:25.470 --> 04:28.270
Sigma's powerful because he has no memories?

04:28.570 --> 04:31.750
That waitress at the shop would
be the strongest ever, then.

04:31.750 --> 04:34.650
She always forgets my orders.

04:34.650 --> 04:37.460
No matter how committed Sigma is,

04:37.460 --> 04:40.160
the Hunting Dogs are in a
totally different league.

04:40.560 --> 04:42.000
League?

04:42.000 --> 04:45.520
It's not just the Hunting Dogs
that are in a separate league.

04:45.520 --> 04:50.100
Even you and I are in a far
lower league than Sigma.

04:50.100 --> 04:54.380
Sorrowful music runs through Sigma's veins.

04:54.690 --> 04:57.050
His alienation is absolute.

04:57.050 --> 05:01.520
The Sky Casino is the only thing
that shares that with him.

05:01.520 --> 05:03.530
He can't afford to lose it.

05:04.060 --> 05:05.020
No...

05:05.020 --> 05:06.490
That's right.

05:06.490 --> 05:11.500
Sigma was born three years ago when
he was written into the book.

05:11.500 --> 05:13.550
Just like that, out of nothing.

05:14.010 --> 05:14.880
Impossible.

05:15.290 --> 05:18.590
Can such a thing really be called human?

05:21.590 --> 05:24.090
Would you not like a home?

05:24.820 --> 05:27.370
He gave himself a name.

05:27.860 --> 05:29.100
"Sigma."

05:29.710 --> 05:34.550
He finally has just one place
to call home: the Sky Casino.

05:35.540 --> 05:38.260
Good day, mister manager.

05:38.570 --> 05:40.680
Are you ready to surrender?

05:42.490 --> 05:43.900
I'm not.

05:44.370 --> 05:45.990
I never could be.

05:45.990 --> 05:48.460
Don't expect me to give you much time.

05:48.460 --> 05:54.960
I'm about to destroy that communication
device and save the world, after all.

05:54.960 --> 05:57.330
This device is a mere terminal.

05:57.900 --> 06:02.910
The trigger signal cannot be stopped
without this key to override it.

06:02.910 --> 06:04.480
I thought so.

06:04.480 --> 06:06.050
All right, then.

06:06.390 --> 06:07.870
Don't get me wrong.

06:07.870 --> 06:09.420
I'll give you the key.

06:11.540 --> 06:15.500
To be honest, I wanted to
just run away in tears.

06:16.500 --> 06:19.470
But if I don't stop the Hunting Dogs,
the casino will be ruined.

06:20.490 --> 06:23.160
The enemy is the strongest
special force in the country.

06:23.400 --> 06:25.780
And I'm just an ordinary man.

06:26.750 --> 06:27.420
But...

06:31.330 --> 06:32.240
Open fire!

06:33.410 --> 06:34.900
I will prevail!

06:43.330 --> 06:44.340
Kyouka-chan!

06:45.330 --> 06:47.220
I hear fighting from the lower decks.

06:47.220 --> 06:48.430
It's starting.

06:48.430 --> 06:49.670
It must be the Hunting Dogs.

06:50.340 --> 06:52.440
They've gotten here a lot
sooner than I expected.

06:52.440 --> 06:56.150
We need to join the fight soon,
or Dazai-san's plan will be ruined.

06:59.940 --> 07:03.430
You ought to be able make it to the
bottom floor using your claws.

07:04.440 --> 07:05.430
Go, please.

07:06.200 --> 07:07.710
Leave this to me.

07:14.530 --> 07:15.510
Impossible!

07:15.510 --> 07:16.870
She's deflecting them with her bare hands?!

07:17.520 --> 07:21.570
No, not even the Hunting Dogs could
hold up against this for long.

07:27.080 --> 07:27.920
What?!

07:28.870 --> 07:30.430
Cooking knives?!

07:30.430 --> 07:31.840
She must have stolen them from the kitchen!

07:33.380 --> 07:34.350
I'm not done yet!

07:34.350 --> 07:36.360
I can start up another turret!

07:38.590 --> 07:40.060
Forget it.

07:40.060 --> 07:43.030
You never had a chance to begin with.

07:43.740 --> 07:45.160
You're right.

07:45.550 --> 07:49.060
As you can see, I'm not much of a man.

07:49.770 --> 07:52.980
But all is according to plan!

07:53.340 --> 07:54.740
A directed resonance gun!

08:00.140 --> 08:02.730
I doubt you can lift a finger.

08:02.710 --> 08:07.460
The acoustic waves are entering through your
ears and creating bubbles inside your brain.

08:07.460 --> 08:10.370
And this one's been modified
to be five time as powerful.

08:10.710 --> 08:12.240
See that, Hunting Dog?

08:12.600 --> 08:13.820
This...

08:13.820 --> 08:16.640
All this is the power of my determination!

08:19.790 --> 08:20.780
Impossible!

08:21.290 --> 08:22.470
How can you stand?!

08:23.040 --> 08:27.470
This output level would wear down
even a Hunting Dog's brain!

08:27.470 --> 08:29.590
The power of your determination, you say?

08:30.590 --> 08:32.280
Then, let me ask...

08:32.280 --> 08:36.330
Why do you think you're the only one

08:38.470 --> 08:40.070
who has determination?!

08:41.390 --> 08:43.170
The injury in her ear...

08:43.610 --> 08:44.550
It can't be...

08:44.550 --> 08:50.540
Did she destroy her own ear canal to
stop the sound from infiltrating her?!

08:50.540 --> 08:53.390
I have a story for you.

08:53.890 --> 08:56.320
The Hunting Dogs' superhuman physical prowess

08:56.320 --> 08:59.540
is the result of surgery carried out
by doctors with special abilities.

08:59.540 --> 09:02.780
But the inhuman nature of the
surgeries made them such that,

09:02.780 --> 09:07.980
if we miss even one of the monthly follow-up
surgeries, our flesh rots and we die.

09:07.980 --> 09:10.960
Why would you go so far?

09:10.960 --> 09:13.240
We are the manifestation
of this country's order.

09:13.240 --> 09:18.000
Without order, those who thrive through
violence would conquer the people.

09:18.000 --> 09:20.900
I will <i>not</i> tolerate such a vile world.

09:21.270 --> 09:25.220
Thus, the Hunting Dogs
employ maximum violence.

09:25.220 --> 09:31.510
As slaves of society, we will not spare
even our own selves from order's flame!

09:34.580 --> 09:36.460
This is your final warning.

09:36.460 --> 09:38.080
Surrender.

09:38.080 --> 09:39.530
I refuse.

09:39.530 --> 09:43.420
There's no wall that even a mediocre man
can't overcome, with enough desperation.

09:43.420 --> 09:44.860
You're right.

09:44.860 --> 09:47.980
The desperation of a mediocre
man is indeed terrifying.

09:47.980 --> 09:49.360
But what is there beyond that?

09:50.810 --> 09:52.080
Do you not understand?

09:52.390 --> 09:55.880
Beyond the wall that a mediocre
man overcomes with desperation

09:55.880 --> 09:59.180
is a battle against a genius
who is equally desperate.

09:59.180 --> 10:02.840
A battle where desperation
holds no relative value.

10:03.710 --> 10:05.990
Welcome to our world.

10:10.760 --> 10:12.600
I understand it well.

10:12.990 --> 10:15.120
I don't stand a chance.

10:15.120 --> 10:17.540
Both the casino and I are doomed.

10:17.540 --> 10:21.380
Then I will save at least one!

10:21.380 --> 10:22.550
What?!

10:23.880 --> 10:27.530
Is he going to die with me
to protect the casino?!

10:34.670 --> 10:35.890
You aren't getting away!

10:35.890 --> 10:39.190
Where does this man get
so much strength from?

10:39.600 --> 10:41.440
I can't catch him alive.

11:00.600 --> 11:01.860
Be careful.

11:04.140 --> 11:08.080
We're at the casino's foundation,
above the power box.

11:08.080 --> 11:10.310
If you fall again, you're done.

11:10.970 --> 11:12.530
You're with the Detective Agency.

11:13.020 --> 11:14.950
Why did you save me?

11:14.950 --> 11:17.690
Why? Why else?

11:17.690 --> 11:20.850
The only way we can save the
Agency is to obtain the page.

11:21.580 --> 11:24.670
And you know where it is.

11:24.670 --> 11:27.680
Even if I did, do you
think I would tell you?

11:27.680 --> 11:28.770
I do.

11:29.580 --> 11:30.040
Sakaguchi Ango

11:30.290 --> 11:35.380
Using my ability, I can read
the page's location from your mind.

11:35.380 --> 11:37.570
It's the man from Special Ops!

11:38.180 --> 11:41.880
Sorry, but I've already taken measures
to protect against your ability.

11:41.880 --> 11:45.710
Then we'll simply have to hurt
you until you want to talk.

11:46.190 --> 11:48.260
You're the man who stabbed Chief Taneda.

11:48.260 --> 11:50.060
I have no intention

11:50.060 --> 11:51.650
of showing mercy.

11:53.140 --> 11:55.010
I didn't intend to stab him.

11:55.710 --> 11:58.040
I only wanted to threaten him.

11:59.620 --> 12:01.380
Ask whatever you want.

12:01.380 --> 12:02.780
I can't do this anymore.

12:03.130 --> 12:09.290
In the end, I never even
found my reason for being.

12:11.110 --> 12:14.200
Atsushi-kun, this is the final mission.

12:14.200 --> 12:16.540
Please deliver Sigma to the surface.

12:16.980 --> 12:18.170
Understood.

12:22.060 --> 12:22.980
No way!

12:23.740 --> 12:25.040
Here?

12:25.790 --> 12:28.530
Is this the moment you choose, Fyodor?

12:34.740 --> 12:36.230
Atsushi-kun, be careful!

12:37.000 --> 12:40.110
He's going to kill you to save his own!

12:41.060 --> 12:42.490
Guilty.

12:53.000 --> 12:55.050
Sigma-san! Be strong!

12:55.520 --> 12:56.970
It's fine.

12:57.430 --> 13:00.700
I had a feeling it would end like this.

13:03.730 --> 13:05.610
Atone for your sins.

13:18.820 --> 13:21.890
Let me go. You'll die, too.

13:21.890 --> 13:22.700
No!

13:23.280 --> 13:26.830
You never knew your reason for being?

13:26.830 --> 13:30.900
Those are words that can never
be a person's last! It's wrong!

13:34.590 --> 13:37.120
You're a kind man.

13:38.470 --> 13:39.710
But it's fine.

13:39.710 --> 13:40.310
No!

13:40.540 --> 13:43.980
I've done all I can as an ordinary man.

13:51.930 --> 13:54.230
Lucy-san, please look down.

13:54.570 --> 13:55.500
What?

13:55.500 --> 13:56.260
Now!

13:58.300 --> 13:59.260
It's him!

13:59.530 --> 14:02.400
Please throw him a rope or
something he can grab onto.

14:02.400 --> 14:04.660
I don't have anything.

14:04.660 --> 14:05.480
But...

14:05.890 --> 14:08.520
No, I have a way, though.

14:09.070 --> 14:11.120
You'd better gather my
bones if I fall, though.

14:12.150 --> 14:14.580
Atsushi!

14:17.460 --> 14:19.000
Transport!

14:25.460 --> 14:27.150
Ow, ow...

14:29.120 --> 14:31.210
Looks like we made it.

14:31.210 --> 14:32.520
Thanks.

14:32.520 --> 14:33.420
You saved me—

14:33.940 --> 14:34.900
Look out!

14:39.160 --> 14:40.670
How did he get in here?

14:42.530 --> 14:44.090
A thin string of blood.

14:44.520 --> 14:48.530
He must have tied this to me so
he would be transported with us.

14:49.590 --> 14:50.540
This is bad.

14:51.060 --> 14:52.480
No, it's over.

14:52.740 --> 14:55.800
Welcome to my kingdom.

15:01.330 --> 15:05.290
As long as you're in this room,
you can't hurt Anne.

15:14.300 --> 15:17.070
Yes! I finally captured him!

15:17.070 --> 15:18.390
We win!

15:18.390 --> 15:20.810
No. We've lost.

15:21.260 --> 15:23.400
We've let Sigma die.

15:23.970 --> 15:26.470
We no longer have a way to locate the page.

15:27.060 --> 15:27.860
Worse...

15:28.720 --> 15:31.900
The Hunting Dogs have seen
you work to save Sigma.

15:33.120 --> 15:38.290
They will perceive that as the
Agency cooperating with fellow terrorists.

15:38.730 --> 15:42.230
I'm afraid this was all
according to Fyodor's plan.

15:43.930 --> 15:45.120
We've lost.

15:47.660 --> 15:49.350
You're unbelievable.

15:49.650 --> 15:51.680
I haven't done anything.

15:52.100 --> 15:54.800
I simply sat here and prayed.

15:55.320 --> 15:57.990
Prayers alway reaches God.

15:58.300 --> 16:01.210
So even the coin bombs were a decoy.

16:01.650 --> 16:06.100
Just a means to draw the Hunting Dogs
and the Detective Agency to the casino.

16:06.720 --> 16:08.020
Why?

16:10.780 --> 16:13.460
It's more beautiful that way, is it not?

16:14.260 --> 16:17.210
Gotta gain information on the terrorists.

16:19.670 --> 16:21.070
What is this?

16:27.150 --> 16:32.380
I will share the truth of the case with you,
in hopes that you are a sensible person.

16:32.380 --> 16:33.880
The Detective Agency!

16:33.070 --> 16:38.140
The masterminds behind the terrorist attacks
are the five Gifteds, the Decay of the Angels.

16:38.140 --> 16:42.370
They've stolen a device known as
"the page" that amends reality.

16:42.370 --> 16:44.110
They've smeared the
Detective Agency with their crime, and—

16:45.730 --> 16:50.750
I suppose you've been spreading
a web of conspiracies yourself.

16:50.750 --> 16:53.700
But God prefers perfection and harmony.

16:54.270 --> 17:00.830
Thus, in accordance with God's will,
I added a particular line to the page.

17:03.500 --> 17:05.450
Tachihara, have you found anything?

17:05.790 --> 17:08.280
And as the final stage of their plan,

17:08.280 --> 17:11.290
they intend to write the demise
of the state onto the page.

17:12.030 --> 17:14.660
That is the full story of the
worldwide terrorism attack, and...

17:14.660 --> 17:16.770
Tachihara, what's the matter?

17:16.770 --> 17:18.010
No. Nothing.

17:18.540 --> 17:21.790
Just more false information meant
to throw off the investigation.

17:23.580 --> 17:27.160
A modification to ensure they don't believe
in the Detective Agency's innocence?

17:27.160 --> 17:27.990
Yes.

17:27.990 --> 17:32.270
All law enforcement and investigative
bodies that happen upon evidence

17:32.270 --> 17:38.840
of the Detective Agency's entrapment
will dismiss it without consideration.

17:38.840 --> 17:41.050
That's what I wrote in the page.

17:41.710 --> 17:48.390
In other words, the plot to get the Hunting Dogs
on your side was futile to begin with.

17:48.780 --> 17:51.830
Infiltrate the Port Mafia again?!

17:51.830 --> 17:52.660
Yep.

17:52.660 --> 17:54.580
I've gotten in touch with the surface.

17:55.090 --> 17:59.490
The Detective Agency has thoroughly
crossed a line with the coin bombs.

17:59.490 --> 18:03.180
This is no longer a state's criminal matter.

18:03.630 --> 18:05.740
The whole world's going to be on their ass.

18:06.400 --> 18:10.010
Which means we have to be
the ones to catch them.

18:10.380 --> 18:13.610
Tachihara, infiltrate the Mafia once more

18:13.610 --> 18:17.920
and find out where the last two
Detective Agency members have run off to.

18:21.960 --> 18:23.490
Are you reluctant?

18:23.490 --> 18:24.130
No.

18:24.130 --> 18:29.290
It's just that, these days, I get strangely
annoyed dealing with the Mafia.

18:30.940 --> 18:32.240
You?

18:32.590 --> 18:37.300
You're practically born to do undercover
investigations, with your special ability.

18:37.740 --> 18:42.760
You did it when you eliminated the Mafia
members who were aiding the Detective Agency.

18:45.250 --> 18:46.470
I...

18:51.330 --> 18:54.720
Tachihara. You made it.

18:54.720 --> 18:56.860
I heard you were stabbed in the gut.

18:56.860 --> 18:59.380
It wasn't as bad as I thought.

18:59.380 --> 19:01.550
The same as us, then.

19:01.550 --> 19:02.510
Yeah.

19:02.510 --> 19:06.310
Despite my spectacular bloodshed,
the wounds were rather shallow.

19:06.800 --> 19:10.770
It was as though the attack was an act.

19:11.350 --> 19:15.500
What's the point if we're both alive
because we were going easy on each other?

19:16.940 --> 19:20.130
Y-You bastard!

19:20.130 --> 19:21.600
Hey, old man...

19:22.850 --> 19:25.940
Do you think I'm cut out for the Port Mafia?

19:38.530 --> 19:41.540
You don't know anything about God, do you?

19:43.360 --> 19:45.060
I'm listening.

19:45.060 --> 19:47.380
Perfection and harmony?

19:47.780 --> 19:52.080
God cares more about your
pores than he does that.

19:52.780 --> 19:55.550
He's famous for his
coincidences and absurdism.

19:55.950 --> 19:57.890
I've seen it countless times.

19:58.630 --> 20:04.780
No matter how masterfully you devise
your schemes, where we are is here.

20:05.420 --> 20:07.540
A prison at the ends of the earth.

20:07.910 --> 20:12.990
The ones that run the world are,
in fact, the ones who howl,

20:12.990 --> 20:15.870
run, and shed blood in incidental storms.

20:16.250 --> 20:22.230
You and I are powerless in the
face of their intense spirits.

20:23.400 --> 20:25.790
Do you know what that means?

20:26.730 --> 20:31.750
Tachihara, you are mafia among mafia.

20:26.990 --> 20:31.750
Tachihara,

20:29.120 --> 20:31.750
you are mafia among mafia.

20:32.920 --> 20:36.710
Your rashness, your hotheadedness,
your reckless valor...

20:37.620 --> 20:41.980
You're a model for the
rest of the Port Mafia.

20:42.520 --> 20:44.960
Why am I feeling this way?

20:45.330 --> 20:49.510
I infiltrated the Port Mafia to
take revenge for my brother...

20:50.490 --> 20:51.510
No...

20:50.640 --> 20:53.520
No...

20:51.510 --> 20:53.150
That's an excuse.

20:51.850 --> 20:53.520
That's an excuse.

20:53.690 --> 20:56.530
I wanted to become someone...

20:57.000 --> 20:59.730
Someone who was neither my brilliant
brother or his opposite.

21:00.650 --> 21:04.710
That's why I spared the doctor...

21:16.690 --> 21:17.770
Tachihara.

21:22.730 --> 21:26.560
I'm sorry about your brother.

21:27.500 --> 21:29.940
The freaking Detective Agency...

21:29.940 --> 21:31.900
Vicious terrorists...

21:32.280 --> 21:34.880
What the hell is wrong with these people?

21:35.400 --> 21:38.090
The Detective Agency will not relent.

21:38.390 --> 21:43.150
If it'll prove the organization's innocence,
they'll abandon their lives.

21:43.690 --> 21:47.850
A guilty verdict would not stand against
them when they forfeit their lives.

21:47.850 --> 21:50.120
They have only an innocent verdict or death.

21:50.120 --> 21:53.470
The world is already
convinced of their guilt.

21:53.960 --> 21:57.450
But I'm not so.

21:57.710 --> 21:59.250
At the very least,

21:59.250 --> 22:02.640
the boss has believed the Detective Agency
to be innocent from the beginning.

22:02.970 --> 22:07.160
I can't imagine he'd ever trust the Detective
Agency on gut feeling or out of sympathy.

22:08.190 --> 22:09.590
Hey, you guys...

22:10.420 --> 22:12.340
What do you think of the Detective Agency?

22:12.800 --> 22:15.580
Do you think they're actually terrorists?

22:16.010 --> 22:18.570
Did you hurt your head
or something, Tachihara?

22:19.790 --> 22:23.890
The truth about the Port Mafia
ought to be obvious to anyone.

22:24.610 --> 22:25.750
Right, Gin?

22:25.750 --> 22:26.360
Yes.

22:26.830 --> 22:28.750
It isn't even worth considering.

22:29.290 --> 22:31.360
The Detective Agency aren't terrorists.

22:31.360 --> 22:32.980
It's preposterous.

22:33.780 --> 22:39.540
Tachihara, if you're Port Mafia,
it ought to be obvious to you, too.

22:40.360 --> 22:42.650
Of course.

22:42.650 --> 22:45.590
The answer is crystal clear.

22:45.590 --> 22:47.550
Fyodor: "All law enforcement and investigative bodies

22:45.590 --> 22:47.550
that happen upon evidence of the Detective Agency's

22:45.590 --> 22:47.550
entrapment will dismiss it without consideration."

22:47.940 --> 22:49.810
What the hell am I doing?

22:51.560 --> 22:54.460
There's no way the Armed Detective
Agency are terrorists.

22:54.460 --> 22:57.110
The government's got the wrong people!

22:57.730 --> 23:00.170
We have to persuade the government!

23:02.160 --> 23:03.930
You're correct.

23:03.930 --> 23:06.420
Humans are sinful and foolish.

23:07.220 --> 23:12.940
But they aren't quite
as boring as you think.

23:23.260 --> 23:25.250
There's the point where it ends.

23:27.170 --> 23:28.180
What's that?

23:33.250 --> 23:37.020
A'ight, time for some resurrection magic!

23:37.590 --> 23:39.210
Oh, so fun!
